{
 "_doc": "CF-THE-SHARD-AXIS-IS-MEASURED-FIRST (GREAT REMATCH, Drew 2026-09-01). Built by GROUP BY over the live sold_comps container, not assumed. Year alone is NOT an axis: 2024=2,711,283 / 2025=2,629,991 / 2023=1,457,497 / 2026=1,268,434 against an even 32-slot share of 510,509 -- a 6.6x spread that would leave one runner working 6x as long as another. The axis is composite in three levels, each used only when the level above is still over a share: (1) cardYear, every year that fits rides whole; (2) + sport class (baseball / football / basketball / pokemon / other) on the four heavy years, since 2025 baseball alone is 1,262,342; (3) + sha1(id) % parts on a unit still over a share, which is uniform by construction. 158 units packed longest-first into 32 slots. rematch-sold-comps.cjs reads this file and its banner echoes this slot's units and their measured rows. `rows` is the count AT CAPTURE and is an expectation for the banner, never a gate -- ingest legitimately adds rows between the measurement and a run.",
